<title>NORWAY: TABLE-UBN H1 PROFITS FALL.</title>
<headline>TABLE-UBN H1 PROFITS FALL.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>				(millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Net interest income	   1,251	vs     1,241</p>
<p> Oper. profit before losses    652	vs	 666</p>
<p> Operating profit		  581	vs	 761</p>
<p> Net profit			  417	vs	 559</p>
<p> Non-interest oper. income     905	vs	 778</p>
<p> Operating costs		 1,504	vs     1,353</p>
<p>Earnings per primary</p>
<p> capital certificate (crowns) 11.33     vs	16.16</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full name of Norway's largest savings bank is Union Bank of Norway (UBN), known locally as Sparebanken NOR. It was expected to post a first-half 1997 operating profit of nearly 700 million crowns, according to six analysts polled by Reuters.</p>
<p>The bank in a statement attributed the drop in profits mainly to a writedown of 93 million crowns of its shares and options in Fokus Bank.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
